  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {白々|しらじら}しい{嘘|うそ} (blatant lie)\n- {白々|しらじら}しい{態度|たいど} (feigned attitude)\n- {白々|しらじら}しい{顔|かお}をする (to put on an innocent face)\nStrongly implies the speaker can see through the pretense. Used when someone's deception or insincerity is painfully obvious.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {空々|そらぞら}しい (similar meaning - forced, unnatural)\n- {白|しら}を{切|き}る (to feign ignorance)\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverb: {白々|しらじら}しく",
